          "markdown": "## transonic wing drag prediction at Mach 0.85: a verification-first computational study\n\nThis study reports a drag coefficient of 0.4264 ± 0.00000336 for transonic wing drag prediction at mach 0.85. The value was obtained on 3 systematically refined meshes; the observed order of accuracy is 2 and the fine-grid Grid Convergence Index is 0.000787 percent. 2 DOI-verified references were retrieved and 1 candidate gap was identified.\n\n### Findings\nThe extrapolated drag coefficient is 0.4264 ± 0.00000336.\n\nThe observed order of accuracy is 2 on 3 meshes, and the fine-grid Grid Convergence Index is 0.000787 percent.\n\n### Candidate gaps\n- mach\n\n### Review status\nrevise — 4 comment(s).\n\n### References\n- [1] C. Author, \"Adjoint-based mesh adaptation for transonic flows,\" Journal of Computational Physics, Vol. 491, 2023, pp. 112001. doi:10.1016/j.jcp.2023.112001\n- [2] A. Author and B. Author, \"Transonic drag prediction on unstructured meshes,\" AIAA Journal, Vol. 62, 2024, pp. 1201–1215. doi:10.2514/1.j060001",
